  "holistic_F_H": -2,
  "section_notes": "S2 is the pivot: the 55 °C / 5% test and numeric per-model results to purchasers satisfy NW-1 and HC-1, but exceeding the limit only triggers corrective action and never stops sales, so Northwind's 6.2%-failing Hearth 10 survives. S5 keeps a mandatory, non-discretionary 8/100k recall trigger with no phase-in, which hits Halcyon's 9.9/100k Ember 8 hard, while S3's six-year retrofit and S4's 36-month suppression exactly track Northwind's and Halcyon's red lines. S1 is strict and symmetric (all incidents within 24h, customer notice 24h, annual reconciliation), and both companies' unreported incidents make it costly to both."
 },
